      "explain": "<strong>Cryptography</strong> is the science of protecting information by converting it into an unreadable form. The original readable message is the <strong>plaintext</strong>; the scrambled form is the <strong>ciphertext</strong>; the process of converting plaintext to ciphertext is <strong>encryption</strong> and the reverse is <strong>decryption</strong>. Both use a <strong>key</strong>. Cryptography is of two kinds: <strong>symmetric</strong> (one shared key) and <strong>asymmetric</strong> (a public/private key pair).",
