        "Packet filtering is <strong>stateless</strong>: each packet is judged alone, with no memory of earlier packets. Fast and cheap, but easily fooled by spoofing.",
        "<strong>Stateful inspection firewall</strong> — keeps a <strong>state table</strong> of active connections and allows replies only for connections that were properly started.",
        "Stateful firewalls are more secure than packet filters and are the common choice today.",
        "<strong>Proxy / application gateway firewall</strong> — works at the <strong>application layer</strong>; it terminates the connection and makes its own request on the client's behalf.",
        "A proxy can inspect the <em>actual content</em> (e.g. block a specific URL or file type) — most secure, but slowest.",
        "<strong>Circuit-level gateway</strong> — works at the session layer, verifying that a connection handshake is legitimate without inspecting content.",
        "Design architectures: <strong>screening router, bastion host, dual-homed host, screened host, screened subnet (DMZ)</strong>.",
        "A <strong>DMZ (demilitarised zone)</strong> holds public servers (web, mail) between two firewalls, separate from the internal network.",
        "A firewall cannot stop attacks that do not pass through it, insider misuse, or malware in already-allowed traffic — it is one layer, not a complete solution."
